    "text_delta": "ed Next Steps\n\n1. **Send a polite, professional follow-up:**  \n   Frame your request around personal development rather than questioning the outcome.\n   > *\"Dear [HR Contact/Hiring Lead], I hope you are having a productive week. Following up on my interview for the Head of Structural Engineering role, I would greatly appreciate any brief notes or feedback the panel might have regarding areas where I can strengthen my profile for future leadership roles. Thank you again for your time and consideration.\"*\n\n2. **Reflect on the interview focus:**  \n   Assess whether your interview discussions leaned heavily toward technical delivery/past projects, or if they equally addressed winning work, managing clients, and financial group performance.\n\n3. **Protect your industry standing:**  \n   The engineering consultancy world is relatively small. Maintaining a gracious, professional relationship with this firm leaves the door open for future senior openings or collaboration, whereas challenging the panel's gender composition without evidence will close doors quickly.\n",
